  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\n**Symptom**:\r\nWhen attempting to federate with matrix.org by trying to browse it's list of rooms in Element, I get a `401 Unauthorized` in the synapse logs, and `Failed to find any key to satisfy VerifyJsonRequest` in the Element UI. After troubleshooting with @anoadragon453 we determined the issue is firewall related.\r\n\r\n**Cause**:\r\nThe current matrix URLs don't resolve to the correct federation server IPs. In my firewall, whitelisting the IPs of **`matrix.org`** and **`matrix-federation.matrix.org`** (currently resolving to `104.20.20.236` and `104.20.21.236`) still prevents matrix from federating with my homeserver. It turns out that **these are the reverse proxy IPs** and are not the same as those of the federation servers.\r\n\r\n**Solution**:\r\nAttach a public DNS name to `matrix.org`'s federation servers so that those with a strictly firewalled synapse server can properly whitelist them and successfully federate.\r\n\r\nOr, route the matrix federation servers outbound traffic through the existing IPs tied to the DNS of `matrix.org` and `matrix-federation.matrix.org` so that whitelisting these will allow proper federation. \r\n\r\n### Version information\r\n\r\n- **Version**: Synapse 1.27.0\r\n\r\n- **Install method**: package manager\r\n<!-- examples: package manager/git clone/pip  -->\r\n\r\n- **Platform**: Ubuntu 18.04\r\n<!--\r\nTell us about the environment in which your homeserver is operating\r\ndistro, hardware, if it's running in a vm/container, etc.\r\n-->\r\n",
